' @guidance:
' Create or update the PlantUML diagram describing how files tagged with the
' @guidance marker are processed. This is a SEPARATE way of using Ghostwriter
' and is NOT part of the Act/episode functionality.
'
' - Implemented by GuidanceProcessor (extends AIFileProcessor, NOT ActProcessor).
' - Reuses the generic project traversal (module discovery, recursion, match()
'   filtering) but does NOT run Act episodes.
' - Show per-file handling: reviewer lookup by extension, guidance extraction via
'   the @guidance: marker, and the decision logic (guidance found / skip).
' - Show prompt composition, provider dispatch, and the report (getReport())
'   which is distinct from the Act pipeline getResults().
' - Keep the diagram readable; prefer clear partitions/swimlanes over clutter.

@startuml
title Ghostwriter - @guidance Tag File Processing (standalone mode, not an Act)

skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F5F7FA
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EDF7ED
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #999999

|#E8EEF7|GuidanceProcessor (init)|
start
:new GuidanceProcessor(rootDir, genai, configurator);
:loadReviewers()
- ServiceLoader<Reviewer>
- index reviewers by normalized file extension;

|#E8EEF7|AbstractFileProcessor (inherited traversal)|
:scanFolder(projectDir);
:projectLayout = getProjectLayout(projectDir);

partition "Module traversal (inherited)" {
  note right
    Modules from ProjectLayout.getModules()
    are recursed into (each re-enters scanFolder).
    processModule() only recurses when the
    configured scan `path` matches / is inside
    the module. NO Act episodes are involved.
  end note
  :recurse into matching modules -> scanFolder(moduleDir);
}

|#EDF3EC|GuidanceProcessor.processParentFiles|
:children = listFiles(projectDir);
:remove children that are module dirs
(isModuleDir) or that do not match();

repeat :next file (child);

  |#FDF3E7|GuidanceProcessor.processFile|
  if (match(file, projectDir)?) then (yes)

    partition "Guidance extraction (parseFile)" {
      :extension = FilenameUtils.getExtension(file);
      :reviewer = getReviewerForExtension(extension);
      if (reviewer == null?) then (yes)
        :guidance = null
        (unsupported file type);
      else (no)
        :guidance = reviewer.perform(projectDir, file)
        - scan comments for "@guidance:" marker
        - preserve marker comments in place;
      endif
    }

    if (guidance != null?) then (yes)
      :prompt = guidance;
      :call process(...);
    else (no)
      :skip file (perform = null);
    endif

    if (guidance != null?) then (yes)

      |#EDF7ED|process(...) -> provider|
      partition "process(...)" {
        :assemble prompt =
        instructions (or guidance_sys_instructions)
        + guidance_rules
        + guidance;
        :send to Genai provider (AIFileProcessor);
        :perform = provider output;
        :append { file, message } to report (getReport());
      }
      note right
        getReport() is specific to guidance mode and is
        DISTINCT from the Act pipeline's getResults().
      end note

      |#FDF3E7|GuidanceProcessor.processFile|
      if (perform is not blank?) then (yes)
        :log provider output;
      endif
    endif

  else (no)
    :skip file;
  endif

repeat while (more files?) is (yes)
->no;

|#E8EEF7|GuidanceProcessor|
stop

legend right
  @guidance tag processing (standalone mode):
  * NOT part of Act/episode functionality; GuidanceProcessor
    extends AIFileProcessor, not ActProcessor.
  * Instructions live INSIDE the file as a "@guidance:" comment
    (constant GUIDANCE_TAG_NAME); the marker must remain unchanged
    so runs stay idempotent/repeatable.
  * Reviewers (ServiceLoader) extract guidance by file extension.
  * Per file: guidance found -> dispatch;
    else skip.
endlegend

@enduml
